WEBVTT

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:05.810
<b>Earth Defense Club (lol)</b>

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:09.390
Mornin'...

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:10.650
Heya.

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:10.650
Good day.

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:16.820
There's something you don't see every day...

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:18.160
What is it?

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.340
Yumoto just sighed!

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.620
What?

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.620
No way!

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.020
What?

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.460
I can sigh sometimes, too...

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:26.700
Can not.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:27.660
Yeah, you can't.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.360
Can't.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:29.210
You cannot.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:31.000
What happened?

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.760
Does it have anything to do with VEPPer?

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.220
No, I don't care about that.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:40.890
Wombat's been getting more careless with 
how he treats Mr. Tawarayama lately.

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:42.810
I believe he's always been that way.

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:44.750
So rude to a dead person.

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:46.230
He is not dead!

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:47.810
He's just in sleep mode!

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:49.360
What is he, a computer?

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:52.490
So why are you sighing, Yumoto?

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:56.780
Something important to me is going away.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:58.430
Something important to you?

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:00.240
Not Wombat?

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.350
I'm curious.

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:02.120
What is it?

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.710
This isn't a sex thing, is it?

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:07.170
Why are you asking so nervously?

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:08.560
It's not a sex thing!

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:10.030
It's Binan Land!

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:12.300
They're tearing it down!

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:15.090
Oh.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.760
What kind of hum-drum reaction is that?!

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.390
I just haven't heard that name in so long.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:24.350
He's right.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.600
<b>Notice About Closing of Binan Land</b>

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.600
<b>To all our regular patrons, we must regrettably
 cease operations. We thank you for your 
loyal devotion all these years.
Binan Land Staff</b>

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:28.070
It says Binan Land is closing 
at the end of the month.

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:29.480
<b>Binan Land
Bringing You Tons of Fun!</b>

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:29.480
Well, go figure.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.820
I don't know a single couple who went 
there that didn't break up afterwards.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:35.820
That's your standard?

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:39.070
Well, if you're going on a date, it's 
gotta be that You-Know-What-land or Sea.

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:43.080
That's their brand. Young or old, 
boy or girl, anyone can enjoy it.

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:46.130
But Binan's just got the 
sad old ferris wheel,

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:49.160
the sad kid's coaster, and that's about it.

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:50.400
And that other thing!

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.500
The sad little merry-go-round!

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:54.000
Wait a minute.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.470
It says they did a hero show at one point, too.

00:01:57.470 --> 00:01:58.430
Seriously?

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:03.890
But "they were so scary, they stopped 
after one performance," it says.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.980
What's there to be scared of in a hero show?

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:07.690
And they only held one?

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.780
So you have a choice between sad or scary?

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:12.820
What a meeting of extremes!

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:14.500
You're all so mean, Senpai!

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.530
Stop calling it sad!

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:18.600
Binan Land...

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:21.490
There's something familiar about that name...

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.500
You don't have to humor him.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:25.180
This is how the world works.

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:26.700
Consider it an education.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.290
You stupid-dupid numbat senpai!

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:35.940
Were we too hard on him?

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:38.010
He did say it was important to him...

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:40.430
Just what is a numbat, anyway?

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.980
Maybe he meant dingbat?

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:45.500
Is a dingbat even a real thing?

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:48.680
He could have also meant 
nimrod or numbskull, too.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:50.080
I see.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.270
Yumoto quality.

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:54.860
Either way, we were probably too hard on him.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:56.220
Yeah...

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:00.060
Binan Land...

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.550
I'm just sure I've heard that name...

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:03.480
I told you, forget it!

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:39.800
Days of Love and Acclaim

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:43.220
Stupidity might be the 
strongest thing there is.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:45.180
What I really can't stand is

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:48.970
<b>Foolish</b>

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:48.970
how astronomically lame they 
are compared to Gora-san.

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:50.690
You're so right.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:53.480
I'd like them to disappear 
without a single particle remaining.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:56.310
I hate lame things, too.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:02.530
<b>Junya Entaro</b>

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:00.530
 It's an honor to be here.

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:01.580
That reminds me.

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:04.490
 Binan Land is finally closing, you know?

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:08.670
That place was just the lamest, right?

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:11.900
It never changed or improved, 
just gathered rust.

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:15.100
I'm so glad it's going away!

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:23.760
Did you just call Binan Land lame?

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.920
You're the one who doesn't understand!

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:28.200
We're going to teach you...

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.460
...the wonders of Binan Land.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:36.600
Those senpai of mine are just the worst!

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:38.990
Binan Land?

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:41.070
I had a rough time there...

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:41.940
Huh?

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:44.650
Bro, you're down on it, too?

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:47.400
Goodness, I nearly burned to death.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:49.240
At Binan Land?

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:52.820
Though, looking back,
 it's become a good memory.

00:05:56.150 --> 00:05:57.920
Yumoto-kun!

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:00.180
We're very sorry!

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:02.000
Let's go play!

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.940
We're here! We're here!

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:09.010
<b>Last Day</b>

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.260
It's Binan Land! Yay!

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:07.420
He sure is excited.

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:09.010
You're not excited enough, En-chan.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:13.500
But are you sure you want 
to pay my entry fee?

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:17.970
We're splitting your ticket, 
so it's only 480 yen each.

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:19.710
480 yen?!

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:20.920
That's a lot of money!

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:21.880
Just take it.

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:23.010
Thanks!

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:25.040
I thought this might happen,

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:28.780
so Bro made me some Bomb Rice Balls!

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:31.100
When you go to an amusement park, 
you need ones with pickled plums,

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:33.220
tuna mayo, bonito flakes, hard-boiled egg,

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:35.990
fried chicken and vinegar-miso onions!

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:40.280
I thought I heard one in there I 
should really be objecting to...

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:41.340
It's good!

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:42.730
Well, forget it.

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:47.180
There's something pretty depressing 
about a trip to the amusement park

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:49.050
with a bunch of guys.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:50.580
Oh, really?

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:52.250
I find it refreshing.

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:54.640
It would be for you, Ryuu.

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:59.720
It's the last day, 
but there aren't many people...

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:00.770
Really?

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:02.060
Isn't this standard?

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:04.300
What ride should we start with?

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:05.160
That's right.

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:07.660
We want rides, not attractions.

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:08.530
Oh! This one!

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:09.790
The Mad Mouse!

00:07:09.790 --> 00:07:12.110
I rode this one seven times, then barfed!

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:13.550
I recommend it!

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:15.120
You're sure it wasn't 
the vinegar-miso onions?

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.140
Why would you ride it until you barf?

00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:21.640
The Mad Mouse is more hard core 
than your standard roller coaster!

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:30.110
See? Hard core, right?

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:32.220
Once was enough for me.

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:33.730
You did it seven times?

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:35.510
I can't believe you survived it.

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:38.210
Well, after I barfed,

00:07:38.210 --> 00:07:40.610
Bro laid me down on a bench, and...

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:44.060
And what happened after that?

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:46.180
What's wrong, Yumoto?

00:07:49.790 --> 00:07:51.610
I'm sorry, Yumoto.

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:54.620
I should have stopped you 
before it got so bad.

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:56.120
It's okay.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:58.280
I just got too excited.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:03.890
Yumoto, I'm sorry.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:09.260
What's wrong, big bro?

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:12.720
Can you wait here a while by yourself?

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:13.570
Y-Yeah.

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:15.220
You're sure you'll be okay?

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:16.400
Yeah.

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:18.680
I'll be okay!

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:19.840
Okay.

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:21.530
I'll be back soon!

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:27.200
Huh?

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:28.690
When did he come back?

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:31.710
I don't remember him coming back...

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:34.980
But if he didn't come back, 
he wouldn't be here now, right?

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:36.670
That's true...

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:41.160
All I have is the memory of feeling 
kind of anxious and lonely...

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:44.790
Well, that axe was clearly 
cause for concern, wasn't it?

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:46.810
Hey.

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:49.950
Do you think that CIDE 
thing Gora-san mentioned...

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:53.280
 Everyone!

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.240
Everyone!

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:59.100
You must Love Making into the Battle Lovers!

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:03.200
Hey, the Doppler effect.

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:06.260
You used to see that in tokusatsu and stuff.

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:09.110
Scenes where they're screaming and you're like 
"where are you even supposed to be yelling from?"

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:10.880
We don't have a choice.

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:12.310
Let's go, too!

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:13.180
Yeah!

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:22.790
I'm tired of spinning around 
and around in the same place!

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:25.470
The limited track.

00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:26.700
The pre-designated movements.

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:28.530
The days of oppression.

00:09:28.530 --> 00:09:31.550
I've had enough of it!

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:33.840
Well, he has a point.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:35.170
I know how he feels.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:37.340
Don't act like you understand!

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:39.920
Love Making!

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:43.670
Love!

00:09:43.670 --> 00:09:46.180
We are, forever, the heirs 
to the throne of love...

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:47.980
Battle Lovers!

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:49.820
Feel the power...

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:51.640
...of love!

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:54.430
Let's go!

00:09:54.430 --> 00:09:57.200
Scarlet Love Lumiere!

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:00.410
W-Wait a minute!

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:04.820
I have over 32 pages of detailed backstory!

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:08.420
Are you sure you want to 
end this that quickly?

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:11.780
Backstory is only effective when 
it's intertwined with the drama!

00:10:11.780 --> 00:10:14.250
All you're doing is padding the narrative!

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:16.970
Th-That's cold...

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:18.320
If you've got a problem,

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:20.940
try changing yourself before 
resenting everything else!

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:22.680
We can change the world!

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:31.020
True Love Attack!

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:43.850
True Love Fountain!

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:58.050
Love is over!

00:10:58.300 --> 00:10:59.130
Okay!

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:02.540
Let's Love Out and ride the Mad Mouse again!

00:11:03.380 --> 00:11:05.390
"We can change the world?"

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:07.180
Stop stealing lines!

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.270
You two...

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:12.600
Galaxy Idols...

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:15.630
The VEPPer!

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:20.020
You five are so uncooperative.

00:11:20.020 --> 00:11:22.670
Earth upbringing breeds poor taste.

00:11:22.670 --> 00:11:24.090
Or rather, no taste at all.

00:11:24.090 --> 00:11:26.670
That's right, I forgot.

00:11:27.140 --> 00:11:28.350
We must apologize.

00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:30.910
Um, VEPP-san...

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:32.000
It's VEPPer!

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:34.680
VEPPer-san.

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:38.780
VEPPer-san, you say you're really big idols,

00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:41.630
and I don't really understand, but okay.

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:46.640
I also get that we're not 
even close to your level.

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:49.470
What are you talking about?

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:52.510
We're not trying to compete with you.

00:11:52.510 --> 00:11:54.630
So could you stop fighting us?

00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:57.930
I feel kind of bad for the people
you turn into monsters, don't you?

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:02.860
So if it might be possible...

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:06.510
Couldn't we just get along from now on?

00:12:09.090 --> 00:12:10.770
Yumoto, really...

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:12.660
Sorry to be harsh, but that's awful.

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:14.880
Huh? How come?

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:18.830
Would you be happy hearing, 
"I won't date you, but can't we be friends"?

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:23.090
It's like saying, "the investment failed,
 so pay me back half the money."

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:25.010
Huh?

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:26.970
Hakone Yumoto...

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:32.220
And the Defense Club...

00:12:32.760 --> 00:12:35.860
We won't forget how you humiliated VEPPer!

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:38.690
You want to get along?

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:40.360
Isn't that funny?

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:42.670
Haru, it is truly funny!

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:45.820
We really want you to disappear!

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:48.410
Without a trace or a memory left behind!

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:52.380
Wait a minute.

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:55.720
There's really just one 
question I want to ask you.

00:12:56.390 --> 00:13:00.030
Why do you hate us in the first place?

00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:01.520
You can't really hate someone

00:13:01.520 --> 00:13:05.180
unless they're at least on your own level...

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:14.190
Maximum Gorar was a person who may 
have become a big brother to us!

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:19.860
<b>Dadacha
Born December 24th 
(adjusting for Earth calendar)
Blood Type B (probably)  Capricorn
Hobbies: Secret
Favorite food: Crickets</b>

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:29.700
<i>This is the end, Maximum Gorar!</i>

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:30.740
Gorar!

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:32.090
Don't worry, Haru!

00:13:32.090 --> 00:13:34.030
Maximum Gorar never loses!

00:13:34.030 --> 00:13:35.360
Y-Yeah...

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:37.120
Maximum Gorar is invincible!

00:13:41.860 --> 00:13:44.070
Huh? M-Maxi...?

00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:44.920
Who's that?

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:47.630
That's Gora's hero name.

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:48.460
Huh?

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:50.810
The Beppu Brothers know Gora-san?

00:13:50.810 --> 00:13:52.100
I'm not sure whether to object

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:55.100
first to the "may have become 
a big brother" line, or...

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:56.560
Everyone!

00:13:57.940 --> 00:14:00.880
I feel I should explain!

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:06.370
Until a while back, Earth played host 
to a battle of love and justice!

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:10.280
The people watched this 
battle and called it...

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:13.660
"Can I Destroy the Earth? 2"

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:13.660
<b>Can I Destroy the Earth? 2</b>

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:18.000
"2" of course means there was a "1"!

00:14:18.180 --> 00:14:19.210
That's my big bro!

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:20.600
That's right!

00:14:20.600 --> 00:14:23.200
The man protecting the Earth 
was the ultimate warrior,

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:26.170
Maximum Gorar!

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:31.620
And we were here!

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:33.560
Right here with Gora-san!

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:38.350
This is taking too long!

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:41.310
That's why I hate exposition episodes!

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:44.400
Forced Memory Transfer!

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:50.570
<b>Binan Land First Hero Show</b>

00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:53.660
To oblivion with this backwater planet!

00:14:56.640 --> 00:14:59.280
Are you not afraid of me?

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:03.210
Well, there's a guy inside the suit, right?

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:06.230
It's hard playing the villain 
in hero shows, huh, Mister?

00:15:10.070 --> 00:15:10.840
What is it?

00:15:12.150 --> 00:15:13.430
I like you!

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:15.440
That sarcasm and cool-headedness.

00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:18.950
You would make fine henchmen for me!

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:21.430
Stranger danger!

00:15:21.430 --> 00:15:22.850
Police!

00:15:22.850 --> 00:15:24.950
Too bad, Earthlings.

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:26.890
I did my research, and found 
out that amusement parks

00:15:26.890 --> 00:15:31.240
are places where the existence 
of aliens is tolerated.

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:35.370
Monsters aren't supposed to be that smart,
you big brute!

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:37.460
I'll teach you one more thing.

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:39.900
Do you know why monsters always 
attack kindergarten buses?

00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:42.250
Because they're on TV shows for kids, right?

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:43.770
Let us go!

00:15:43.770 --> 00:15:45.030
No.

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:47.840
It's because young humans are 
the easiest to brainwash.

00:15:48.150 --> 00:15:51.430
Soon, I will make you worship me.

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:53.020
Will not!

00:15:53.020 --> 00:15:53.890
Someone!

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:55.400
This guy's not acting!

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:56.640
Help us!

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:04.670
Your screams are useless!

00:16:04.670 --> 00:16:06.240
No one can hear you!

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:07.650
 I'm disappointed in you!

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:11.950
Seeing you attack young children!

00:16:13.440 --> 00:16:15.070
Maximum Gorar!

00:16:19.850 --> 00:16:21.330
Let those children go!

00:16:22.510 --> 00:16:23.800
Never!

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:27.170
You're a mere thief, 
attempting to steal my prey!

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:28.420
I will punish you!

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:35.210
Wood-Chopping Beam!

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:36.840
My, my.

00:16:36.840 --> 00:16:37.910
Are you sure you want to do that?

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:40.310
Don't you care what happens 
to these little Earthlings?

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:45.980
It seems you can't touch me 
as long as I have hostages.

00:16:47.260 --> 00:16:50.210
Today you die, Maximum Gorar!

00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:51.440
Take this!

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:01.900
It's hot!

00:17:01.900 --> 00:17:02.900
Don't tell me...

00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:04.910
This is all real?

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:16.910
Rest in peace, Maximum Gorar!

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:18.960
Gorar!

00:17:18.960 --> 00:17:20.930
Wake up! You have to wake up!

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:22.640
Gorar, wake up!

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:25.250
Maximum Gorar!

00:17:26.300 --> 00:17:27.640
It can't be...

00:17:27.640 --> 00:17:29.520
I don't like this plot twist.

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:30.730
It's no use.

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:32.880
Your fate has been decided.

00:17:32.880 --> 00:17:34.600
You cannot change the world.

00:17:34.600 --> 00:17:35.500
Let's go!

00:17:36.060 --> 00:17:38.400
Next week, there will be a new twist!

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:44.370
...can change...

00:17:46.050 --> 00:17:50.540
We... can change... the world.

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:53.340
He still has the strength to stand?

00:17:54.740 --> 00:17:56.550
We <i>can</i> change the world!

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:57.510
What?

00:17:58.200 --> 00:17:58.890
Gorar!

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:01.600
Use the Super Wood-Chopping Axe!

00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:11.400
Super Wood-Chopping Axe!

00:18:18.690 --> 00:18:20.180
Gorar! Thank you!

00:18:20.180 --> 00:18:21.840
Thank you so much!

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:23.220
Thank you for cheering me on.

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:25.120
Take care, you two.

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:27.370
Huh? You're leaving already?

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:28.790
I'm sorry, I have Yumoto...

00:18:29.140 --> 00:18:31.240
I mean, I have a child waiting for me.

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:33.680
Take this.

00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:35.300
It's a Bomb Rice Ball.

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:39.800
There's pickled plums, tuna mayo,

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:41.840
bonito flakes, hard-boiled egg, fried chicken

00:18:41.840 --> 00:18:43.140
and vinegar-miso onions inside.

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:46.950
Make mischief if you must.

00:18:46.950 --> 00:18:48.220
Just grow up big and strong!

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:55.080
I wish he could stay with us forever...

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:55.970
Yeah...

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:02.700
Big bro...

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:04.920
Which means that long ago, Gora-san...

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:06.520
As Maximum Gorar...

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:08.520
...saved the Beppu Brothers?

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:16.050
Wh-What did you say?!

00:19:16.900 --> 00:19:18.830
Tradition, tradition!

00:19:18.830 --> 00:19:20.300
We can't have a major plot twist

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:24.260
without Yufuin-senpai shouting 
"What did you say?!"

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:26.060
That was a great "What did you say?!", too!

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:28.980
Thank you tremendously for your praise.

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:32.230
Ruining our great story with 
their snide comments...

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:36.090
They were unworthy both to hear

00:19:36.090 --> 00:19:39.150
and know about our bond with Gora-san...

00:19:39.550 --> 00:19:41.610
Hey, VEPP Brothers-san.

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:42.820
It's VEPPer!

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:47.090
VEPPer-san, I'm glad you 
like my brother so much,

00:19:47.090 --> 00:19:51.790
but you shouldn't hate my 
senpai because of that.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:53.650
Wrong, Yumoto.

00:19:54.370 --> 00:19:56.910
This is like a complicated 
in-law relationship.

00:19:57.440 --> 00:19:59.880
"I like my husband, but 
I hate my mother-in-law,

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:02.020
and I hate my sister-in-law too."

00:20:02.020 --> 00:20:04.340
The whole "may have been a big brother to us"

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:06.940
indicates a certain unhealthy attachment.

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:10.480
Ryuu, you're surprisingly 
proficient in psychology.

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:12.340
Hey, don't say "surprisingly."

00:20:12.340 --> 00:20:16.060
Anyway, it's viscerally impossible 
for them to get along with us.

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:17.190
It defies logic.

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:20.720
Could you please stop psychoanalyzing us?

00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:23.360
It's extremely aggravating, and creepy, too.

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:24.440
No, no.

00:20:24.440 --> 00:20:26.140
I understand how you feel,

00:20:26.140 --> 00:20:29.090
but that's no reason to pester us.

00:20:29.090 --> 00:20:31.470
Yumoto and Gora-san are brothers.

00:20:31.470 --> 00:20:33.330
That's a fact that can't be changed.

00:20:33.650 --> 00:20:35.750
We may be the Battle Lovers,

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:39.470
but if you don't stop stalking us, we're 
willing to bring the authorities into this.

00:20:39.470 --> 00:20:40.820
What do you mean?

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:45.550
Take them for arbitration or court, 
or get a restraining order, perhaps.

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:49.100
Such graphic language from an 
heir to the throne of love!

00:20:49.300 --> 00:20:52.270
If we can take this to a 
higher authority, we should.

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:53.690
All these battles are tiring me out.

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:57.440
And bringing in a third party 
should cut down on squabbling.

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:01.230
Okay, we'll do that.

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:17.920
<b>Kurotama Bath</b>

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:23.560
I'm so tired.

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:27.930
I'm sorry your last big day at 
Binan Land was such a waste.

00:21:28.230 --> 00:21:29.240
Yeah...

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:30.750
Don't be so sad.

00:21:30.750 --> 00:21:32.310
Memories are forever, right?

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:33.050
That's right.

00:21:33.050 --> 00:21:36.760
Even all that nonsense today might 
turn out to be a good memory.

00:21:36.760 --> 00:21:39.020
Maybe... possibly...

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:40.540
Not convincing.

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:44.540
But yeah, you're right.

00:21:44.540 --> 00:21:47.610
Let's take a bath and cheer ourselves up!

00:21:48.530 --> 00:21:51.120
We're back, Bro Gora!

00:21:51.400 --> 00:21:52.660
Big bro?

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:54.060
Huh?

00:21:54.060 --> 00:21:56.840
He'd usually come right out with his axe...

00:22:01.060 --> 00:22:05.270
Gora-san disappeared with his 
wood-chopping pile unfinished?

00:23:53.800 --> 00:23:58.720
Next Time

00:23:53.800 --> 00:23:58.720
Love is What Matters

00:23:54.860 --> 00:23:56.660
Next time: 
"Love is What Matters!"

00:23:56.660 --> 00:23:57.960
Love Making!
